====Noun====
{{en-noun|loaves}}

# {{senseid|en|bread}} {{q|also {{m|en|loaf of bread}}}} A [[block]] of [[bread]] after [[bake|baking]].
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=8|passage=Philander went into the next room{{...}}and came back with a salt mackerel that dripped brine like a rainstorm. Then he put the coffee pot on the stove and rummaged out a '''loaf''' of dry bread and some hardtack.}}
# Any [[solid]] block of [[food]], such as [[meat]] or [[sugar]].
#* {{RQ:Bacon Sylva Sylvarum|4|passage=sugar-'''loaf'''}}
# {{lb|en|Cockney rhyming slang}} {{ellipsis of|en|loaf of bread}}: the [[brain]] or the [[head]].<ref>{{R:GDoS|id=lueucni|entry=loaf (of bread)|pos=n}}</ref>
#: {{syn|en|q=slang|bonce|noddle|nut|Thesaurus:head}}
#: {{co|en|[[use one's loaf|use one's '''loaf''']]}}
#* {{RQ:Wodehouse Jeeves in the Offing|chapter=VIII and XII|passage=It is frequently said of Bertram Wooster that he is a man who can think on his feet, and if the necessity arises he can also use his '''loaf<!--(as "brain")-->''' when on all fours. [...]<!--ch. XII--> “Why didn't the idiot tell her not to open it?” “It was his first move. ‘I've found a letter from you here, precious,’ she said. ‘On no account open it, angel,’ he said. So of course she opened it.” She pursed the lips, nodded the '''loaf<!--(as "head")-->''', and ate a moody piece of crumpet. “So that's why he's been going about looking like a dead fish.”}}
# A solid block of [[soap]], from which standard [[bar soap]] is [[cut]].
# {{lb|en|cellular automata}} A particular [[still life]] configuration with seven living [[cell]]s.
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=1989-11-20|author=Dean Hickerson|title=Life: glider gun origin|newsgroup=comp.theory.cell-automata|url=https://groups.google.com/g/comp.theory.cell-automata/c/kL6pRsRDG4Q/m/jyweN_cOzTgJ|text=It runs for 17331 generations before stabilizing as 136 blinkers, 109 blocks, 65 beehives, 18 '''loaves''', 18 boats, 7 ships, 4 tubs, 3 ponds, 2 toads, and 40 gliders.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=1992-09-10|author=David Bell|title=Spaceships in Conway's Life (Part 3b)|newsgroup=comp.theory.cell-automata|url=https://groups.google.com/g/comp.theory.cell-automata/c/WNVmyQYN0EQ/m/LJulQ32mFWcJ|text=Running a LWSS into it can produce various debris. One of these reactions produces a '''loaf'''. When the '''loaf''' is properly hit with other LWSSs, it can be pulled backwards.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=1998-01-27|author=Ian Osgood|title=Life: looking for smallest ancestor of a quad-loaf|newsgroup=comp.theory.cell-automata|url=https://groups.google.com/g/comp.theory.cell-automata/c/jAV2m1Ds86E/m/chr7Ia-PjYcJ|text=I am looking for the smallest ancestor of the following four '''loaf''' pattern in Conway's Game of Life:}}
# {{lb|en|informal|slang}} A [[catloaf]].

